<DocsLayout title="Shortest paths" kicker="03 / getting started" description="Build a weighted hopset and compare bounded-hop distances with an exact Dijkstra baseline.">
  <h2>Canonical workflow</h2>
  <pre><code>from reachq import WeightedDigraph
from reachq.hopset import build_hopset_for_sssp
from reachq.invariants import assert_distance_approximation

graph = WeightedDigraph()
graph.add_edge("a", "b", 1)
graph.add_edge("b", "c", 2)
graph.add_edge("a", "c", 10)

hopset, beta = build_hopset_for_sssp(
    graph, epsilon=0.1, random_seed=42, omega=3.0,
)
assert_distance_approximation(
    graph, hopset, source="a", epsilon=0.1, max_hops=20,
)</code></pre>
  <h2>Interpret the result</h2>
  <p><code>epsilon</code> is the allowed multiplicative approximation budget used by the invariant check. <code>beta</code> is a construction quantity, not a wall-clock speedup. The current hopset construction is sequential Python code.</p>
  <p>Use <a href="/reachq/guides/benchmarking.html">benchmarking guidance</a> to record exact and bounded-hop query times separately.</p>
</DocsLayout>
